# Locked agent rules

Follow these rules on every change. Do not edit, delete, rename, or loosen the rule files unless the user explicitly asks to change the rules.

Locked files:

- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
- `AGENTS.md`
- `ai-interpreter/AGENTS.md`
- `ai-interpreter/CLAUDE.md`
- `ai-interpreter/tests/test_ports.py`
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (the jobs and the check name below)

## Writing code

- The screening flow calls `build_interpreter` and `interpret`. It does not name Colab, Kaggle, OpenAI, CUDA, torch, or transformers.
- A new GPU host that serves `scripts/model_server.py` is a new `REMOTE_MODEL_URL`.
- A runtime that is not "call this URL" is a new adapter in `app/services/interpreter.py`, with `engine`, `uses_references`, and `interpret`.
- Keep every CI gate: secret scan, type check, unit and integration, code injection, memory, AI contract. The Kaggle job runs only after those gates, on `main`.
- Leave the check name `all tests passed`. Production deploys on that name.
- Leave the Kaggle job waiting unless the secret `KAGGLE_API_TOKEN` is set. The public defaults are `mwimulebienvenu/viscan-via-train` and `mwimulebienvenu/malhari-via`.
- Do not commit tokens, model weights, or Malhari images.
- Training settings go in `kaggle/viscan-train/train.py` and `ai-interpreter/scripts/finetune_via.py`.

```yaml
# Wrong: drop a gate so the workflow goes green
needs: [backend, frontend]

# Right: every gate still blocks the Kaggle job and the deploy check
needs: [secret-scan, backend, ai-interpreter, ai-avatar, frontend]
```
